<title>UK: UK May oil output lowest since June 1995 - WoodMac.</title>
<headline>UK May oil output lowest since June 1995 - WoodMac.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>British oil production fell to 2.30 million barrels per day (bpd) in May from 2.53 million bpd in April, hitting its lowest level since June 1995, consultants Wood Mackenzie said on Thursday.</p>
<p>May production was also 193,000 bpd down on the corresponding month last year.</p>
<p>&quot;This in part reflects the adoption of a biennial maintenance schedule by many of the operators, with the previous period of heavy maintenance having occurred in 1995,&quot; WoodMac said.</p>
<p>Forties production was restricted by the tying-in of new fields while Brent field output slipped to 110,000 bpd because of maintenance at the Brent Delta and Alpha platforms.</p>
<p>Ninian and Nelson production, by contrast, recovered in May but the latter was still lagging some 20,000 bpd behind its 170,000 bpd average for the last six months of 1996, the consultants said.</p>
